WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.100
Instructor: Before we dive into git aliases,

00:02.100 --> 00:05.580
I wanna talk about the global config file.

00:05.580 --> 00:07.080
We've talked about configuring git

00:07.080 --> 00:09.750
a couple of different times and there are multiple places we

00:09.750 --> 00:12.540
can configure Git, there's actually three.

00:12.540 --> 00:16.860
There is the local config file in every single git repo.

00:16.860 --> 00:18.360
We talked about that, I think,

00:18.360 --> 00:20.233
what, one or two sections ago?

00:20.233 --> 00:22.770
In the .git directory, there is

00:22.770 --> 00:27.770
a file called "config," so settings in there apply

00:27.780 --> 00:31.350
to one repo and just that one local repo.

00:31.350 --> 00:33.930
Then, we have the global git config file

00:33.930 --> 00:36.000
where we can configure settings that will apply

00:36.000 --> 00:39.870
across all repos, but there's actually one level above that,

00:39.870 --> 00:43.890
which I never use, there's a system-wide config file.

00:43.890 --> 00:47.220
If you have multiple users and accounts on one machine,

00:47.220 --> 00:49.710
that system-wide config file would apply

00:49.710 --> 00:52.830
to all of those users, but I just use one account

00:52.830 --> 00:55.260
for the most part, so I configure things globally

00:55.260 --> 00:58.440
if I want them to impact all of my repos.

00:58.440 --> 01:00.660
So we configured things globally early

01:00.660 --> 01:03.360
on using the command line, "git config,"

01:03.360 --> 01:07.650
and then we do --global, and then user.name,

01:07.650 --> 01:10.290
for example, that's one thing that we set,

01:10.290 --> 01:11.850
and then we also did user.email.

01:11.850 --> 01:13.800
I'm just retrieving those values,

01:13.800 --> 01:16.380
but I could change them from the command line,

01:16.380 --> 01:19.410
and when we learn how to make aliases in the next video,

01:19.410 --> 01:20.967
I can do that from the command line.

01:20.967 --> 01:23.340
I'm just adding a new configuration

01:23.340 --> 01:26.760
or I'm changing a setting, but it's kind of annoying

01:26.760 --> 01:28.650
to do it from the command line, for me at least,

01:28.650 --> 01:30.420
I like to see all of my aliases

01:30.420 --> 01:32.730
at once, so we can actually open

01:32.730 --> 01:36.270
up the config file, the global config file.

01:36.270 --> 01:37.710
So where do we look for that?

01:37.710 --> 01:40.140
We saw that the local config file lives

01:40.140 --> 01:43.620
in the .git folder for every repo.

01:43.620 --> 01:47.340
Well, the global config file is called .gitconfig,

01:47.340 --> 01:49.380
it's a hidden file, and it's located

01:49.380 --> 01:51.630
in the Home directory by default.

01:51.630 --> 01:54.570
So we can take a look at it, I could just print it out,

01:54.570 --> 01:58.653
so it's tilde, to reference the home directory, .gitconfig,

01:59.520 --> 02:01.470
and this is what I have in it right now.

02:01.470 --> 02:02.310
I don't think I've really done

02:02.310 --> 02:04.950
a whole lot in this config file.

02:04.950 --> 02:07.228
I've set up, yeah, really not much.

02:07.228 --> 02:10.440
Also, I'll just open it over here. Here we go.

02:10.440 --> 02:14.670
So we have things like user, name is called "Steele,"

02:14.670 --> 02:17.910
so I could change that here, or change my email here,

02:17.910 --> 02:20.550
and this does the exact same thing

02:20.550 --> 02:23.430
that this line did right here

02:23.430 --> 02:26.850
if I were to set user.name to be something else,

02:26.850 --> 02:30.210
so two interfaces that change the same setting,

02:30.210 --> 02:31.530
one from the command line,

02:31.530 --> 02:34.440
it actually changes this file right here.

02:34.440 --> 02:38.550
So if I run this, you'll see it now has been updated.

02:38.550 --> 02:40.860
I didn't change this in the file myself.

02:40.860 --> 02:42.960
This command triggered that change,

02:42.960 --> 02:44.580
but I'm going to go back to what we

02:44.580 --> 02:47.850
had in there and I'm gonna save that, okay?

02:47.850 --> 02:50.100
So there are lots of settings that we can change in here,

02:50.100 --> 02:52.500
just like with the local config files.

02:52.500 --> 02:55.860
It's kind of overwhelming how many things you can update.

02:55.860 --> 02:58.830
Aliases are probably the most important aside

02:58.830 --> 03:00.450
from the basic things like your username

03:00.450 --> 03:04.500
and email as well as setting up your editor.

03:04.500 --> 03:06.000
So I did this early on.

03:06.000 --> 03:07.770
If you recall, I used VS Code,

03:07.770 --> 03:10.320
I set that up, that's what this code is,

03:10.320 --> 03:13.650
that's just the the name that we use to refer to VS Code,

03:13.650 --> 03:16.110
but this could be another editor's name.

03:16.110 --> 03:19.650
That's where we tell Git what editor to use by default,

03:19.650 --> 03:20.850
and so that's the sort of thing we want

03:20.850 --> 03:23.160
to happen globally in all repos.

03:23.160 --> 03:25.320
The same goes for setting up these aliases

03:25.320 --> 03:27.090
that I'll show you in the next video.

03:27.090 --> 03:30.270
